{
  "case_id": "2008-07-608",
  "document_hash": "eeb4de82c86127454caaf4f41e42bb5c3997dd50cddde3e2083f3b259573e2f8",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-608",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eeb4de82c86127454caaf4f41e42bb5c3997dd50cddde3e2083f3b259573e2f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eeb4de82c861-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:53 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2008-07-608",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eeb4de82c86127454caaf4f41e42bb5c3997dd50cddde3e2083f3b259573e2f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eeb4de82c861-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent's conviction for battering his wife is a misdemeanor crime of domestic violence primarily for two reasons: First, the statutory text is most naturally read that way. Second, a contrary reading would defeat Congress's purposes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-608",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eeb4de82c86127454caaf4f41e42bb5c3997dd50cddde3e2083f3b259573e2f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eeb4de82c861-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Well, Respondent says that may be because a lot of people in Congress wanted it to be a dead letter."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-608",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eeb4de82c86127454caaf4f41e42bb5c3997dd50cddde3e2083f3b259573e2f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eeb4de82c861-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: And this was misdemeanor assault and battery, wasn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Saharsky",
      "case_id": "2008-07-608",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eeb4de82c86127454caaf4f41e42bb5c3997dd50cddde3e2083f3b259573e2f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eeb4de82c861-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SAHARSKY: Well, I mean, certainly the offense is this particular case was serious. The charging document reflects that Respondent hit his wife all around the face until it swelled out, kicked her all around her body, kicked here in the ribs --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-608",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eeb4de82c86127454caaf4f41e42bb5c3997dd50cddde3e2083f3b259573e2f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eeb4de82c861-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Wasn't the -- wasn't the statute responding to just that problem, that domestic abuse tended to be charged as misdemeanors rather than felonies?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-608",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eeb4de82c86127454caaf4f41e42bb5c3997dd50cddde3e2083f3b259573e2f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eeb4de82c861-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Does -- does it make clear\nwhether the offense has to be domestic -- a domestic\nviolence offense or whether an ordinary assault offense\nwill qualify if as a matter of fact it was domestic?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-608",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eeb4de82c86127454caaf4f41e42bb5c3997dd50cddde3e2083f3b259573e2f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eeb4de82c861-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But suppose this statute,\nthe one that was enacted, had the word \"if\" before\n\"committed.\" Would that then convey the meaning that\nthe Government is urging? Has as an element use of\nforce, comma, \"if\" committed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Giatrass",
      "case_id": "2008-07-608",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eeb4de82c86127454caaf4f41e42bb5c3997dd50cddde3e2083f3b259573e2f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eeb4de82c861-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GIATRAS: I believe it would have\nbeen -- in 1993, '94 time period, it would have been\nvery difficult -- it would have been, it should have\nbeen very easy to -- to advise Mr. Hayes with respect\nto that issue. Certainly. That he would not have lost his\nrights at that point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-608",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eeb4de82c86127454caaf4f41e42bb5c3997dd50cddde3e2083f3b259573e2f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eeb4de82c861-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: I looked at the\namicus brief filed by the National Network, page 18\nfootnote 53, and I see California, Illinois, Michigan,\nOhio."
    },
    {
